   "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vincentsch/explainroo/tarball/v0.2.0",
   "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vincentsch/explainroo/zipball/v0.2.0",
   "body": "explainroo 0.2 brings more voices, more things a scene can show, and more ways to publish a video.\n\n**Voices and languages**\n\n- Narration in Spanish, French, Italian, Brazilian Portuguese and Hindi as well as English. Set `\"language\": \"es\"` in `video.json`. The Kokoro voices for those languages need espeak-ng installed once.\n- An ElevenLabs voice, or your own recording, as one take or one file per scene. Word timing, cues, captions and checks work the same for every source.\n\n**What a scene can show**\n\n- `s.clip()` plays video clips such as screen recordings, frame-exact, with their sound if you want it.\n- `s.math()` typesets TeX formulas, which are written on in the hand-drawn looks.\n- `s.code()` takes a list of steps and animates code from one version to the next.\n\n**Publishing**\n\n- Every render also writes `.srt` and `.vtt` subtitle files, a cover image, and YouTube chapters when scenes name them.\n- `--format gif`, and `--transparent` WebM or MOV for video editors.\n- `--size` renders one project in several sizes, for example for YouTube and TikTok.\n- `explainroo export` writes a web player that draws the video live, sharp at any size, for docs sites and iframes.\n\n**Product demos and looks**\n\n- `explainroo capture <url>` saves a live site's screenshots, colors, fonts, logo and wording.\n- A project can bring its own look in a JSON file that extends a built-in look. Thanks @mrthommaso for the proposal (#4).\n- `check` suggests a readable color for text with low contrast.\n\n**Fixes**\n\n- Long videos render again: page uploads now go up in pieces (#2, thanks @mrthommaso).\n- On macOS the CLI exits cleanly after loading the speech models (#1, thanks @meminens).\n- Burned-in captions split each sentence into balanced phrases, and the cover leaves them out.\n- The speech check confirms a word written as `{shown|spoken}` when it hears the shown form.\n\nThe videos attached here were made with explainroo. Their sources are in `examples/`:\n\n- `callbacks-to-async-await.mp4`: callbacks, promises and async/await with code steps (midnight look)\n- `circle-area.mp4`: why a circle's area is πr², with formulas (chalk look)\n- `why-is-the-sky-blue-es.mp4`: why the sky is blue, narrated in Spanish (paper look)\n\nAll examples, more videos and the documentation are on https://www.explainroo.com\n",
   "mentions_count": 2
