   "body": "Text that looks sharp in a 1080p still can become unreadable in a smaller video player. This update adds a check for that before upload.\n\n- Run `explainroo check videos/<name> --view-width 854` to flag visible text below 16px at that player width. Camera and group zoom count toward the text size.\n- The agent guide now requires smaller-player checks for Reddit and other feeds, including a 480p still review and a check of the platform's upload.\n- Added `examples/sqlite-demo`, with larger terminal text and only the current command and result on screen. The revised MP4 is attached.\n\nThe check measures text size. It cannot control the playback quality a platform chooses.\n\nValidation: 42 tests pass, including a headless browser test at full and half render scales. The SQLite video has no layout or playback-size warnings, no verification issues, and 99.4% confirmed speech. A rendered Unspar excerpt and still were also checked.\n"
  },
